//@version=6
// Gold cross (PRIVATE TEST VERSION, NOT YET RUN IN TRADINGVIEW)
//
// For YOUR OWN checking only. Do not share this one: a strategy() script lists every trade in the
// Strategy Tester, which shows exactly when it enters and leaves, and it draws both averages.
//
// Put it on a 1-MINUTE XAUUSD chart. It follows docs/sma-cross-spec.md:
//   - Buy / Sell on a fresh cross of the 100-candle average over the 5,000-candle average, on a closed candle.
//   - The opposite cross closes the trade and (inside trading hours) opens the other side: stop-and-reverse.
//   - New trades only 03:30 to 11:00 IST (22:00 to 05:30 UTC). The opposite-cross exit works all day.
//   - Take profit and stop loss as price distances (300 pips = 30.00 USD, 100 pips = 10.00 USD).
// What to compare with the MT5 bot: the list of trade times (Strategy Tester > List of Trades > Export).
// TradingView prices come from a different feed, so expect some crosses to land a candle away.
strategy("Gold cross (private test)", overlay = true, initial_capital = 10000, default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1, pyramiding = 0, calc_on_every_tick = false, commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 0.03)

tpUsd = input.float(30.0, "Take profit (price distance, USD)", minval = 1.0)
slUsd = input.float(10.0, "Stop loss (price distance, USD)", minval = 1.0)
useHours = input.bool(true, "Open trades only 03:30 to 11:00 IST")

fast = ta.sma(close, 100)
slow = ta.sma(close, 5000)
buy = ta.crossover(fast, slow)
sell = ta.crossunder(fast, slow)
inHours = not useHours or not na(time(timeframe.period, "2200-0530", "UTC"))

if buy
    if inHours
        strategy.entry("Buy", strategy.long)       // also closes a short: stop-and-reverse
    else
        strategy.close("Sell", comment = "opposite cross")
if sell
    if inHours
        strategy.entry("Sell", strategy.short)
    else
        strategy.close("Buy", comment = "opposite cross")

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("Buy exit", "Buy", limit = strategy.position_avg_price + tpUsd, stop = strategy.position_avg_price - slUsd)
if strategy.position_size < 0
    strategy.exit("Sell exit", "Sell", limit = strategy.position_avg_price - tpUsd, stop = strategy.position_avg_price + slUsd)

plot(fast, "Fast (100)", color = #2a78d6)
plot(slow, "Slow (5000)", color = #eb6834, linewidth = 2)
